# The repository is stored with LF, and checked out with LF everywhere.
#
# Git for Windows ships with `core.autocrlf=true`, so without this a Windows
# checkout gets CRLF in the working tree and `pnpm format:check` then fails on
# every file in the repository: Prettier's default `endOfLine` is `lf`, and the
# only difference it finds is the line ending. CI runs on Linux, so nothing
# there ever sees it — the first person to hit it is somebody developing on the
# platform this shell is written for.
* text=auto eol=lf
